  "notes": "Modified cash basis village, FYE 9/30/23. Governmental lines from the governmental funds statement p5 Total column; Loan proceeds 685,000 is printed inside Total revenues, so recorded as a receipt line (Loan Proceeds). Contributions and grants 426,909 kept as one line (General 65,859 = Contributions 52,839 + Grant income 12,520 on p10, but Street 361,050 has no printed breakdown). Governmental cash not printed as a roll-forward; fund balances used (369,644 -> 524,479; reconciles). Transfers: in Street 184,000; out General 85,000 + CDA 84,000 + Keno 15,000; business-type Water +15,000 / Trash -15,000 net zero. The all-funds budget schedule p9 prints Transfers in/out 230,000 vs 199,000 in the statements (pp5, 7); recorded nothing from it. Business-type (Water, Sewer, Trash) from p7 by cost type plus principal/interest; disbursements total 173,638 printed on p2 (operating 105,469 + nonoperating 68,169). Proprietary cash flow statement p8 filled. Balance sheet: governmental lines from the governmental funds Balance Sheet p4 (totals equal the government-wide 524,479), business-type from p1. Detail: General Fund departments schedule p10 by department column; the p9 all-funds budget schedule's governmental lines combine all funds (General included) so are not recorded; its Water/Sewer/Trash expenditure lines recorded with budget. Street, Community Development Agency and Keno funds have no schedule of their own. Read pages 1-10 of 10"
